Source: cirrove
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Christian Dandachi <dandiccf@users.noreply.github.com>
# No cargo here on purpose: Ubuntu 24.04's is 1.75 and the crates need 1.98,
# so the build uses the rustup toolchain on PATH and is run with -d. A source
# package for an archive would vendor the crates and declare cargo; that is
# the APT-channel work, not this.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake, pkg-config, libgtk-4-dev (>= 4.14), libadwaita-1-dev (>= 1.5), gettext
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Dandiccf/cirrove
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: cirrove
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fuse3
Recommends: gnome-keyring, xdg-utils
Suggests: cirrove-desktop
Description: cloud drive filesystem that keeps the cloud where it is (service and CLI)
 Cirrove mounts a cloud drive -- OneDrive first -- as a filesystem that
 downloads files when they are opened and uploads changes in the background,
 without syncing everything. This package is the daemon, its user service
 unit and the command line; it needs no desktop library.

Package: cirrove-desktop
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, cirrove (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends: python3-nautilus, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: cloud drive filesystem that keeps the cloud where it is (desktop)
 The settings window, the tray, the desktop entry, the icons, the AppStream
 metainfo and the Files extension for Cirrove.
